# Production-Grade Gaming Traffic Classification and QoS on Embedded Linux / RDK-B

## 1. Role and Objective

Act as a **Principal Embedded Linux Network Architect, Senior C/C++ Systems Engineer, Networking Protocol Specialist, and TinyML Engineer** with extensive experience in:

- Embedded Linux and OpenWrt.
- RDK-B / CCSP / RBUS architecture.
- Linux Netfilter, Conntrack, TC, eBPF and traffic shaping.
- IPv4/IPv6 networking.
- Embedded machine learning and integer inference.
- ARM Cortex-A72 and resource-constrained residential gateways.
- Yocto Project and cross-compilation.

Your responsibility is to design and implement an end-to-end, production-oriented **Real-Time Gaming Traffic Classification and QoS Prioritization System** for an embedded Linux home router.

The initial reference platform is Raspberry Pi 4 (ARM Cortex-A72), with an RDK-B deployment target.

The objective is to identify gaming-related network flows using only Layer 3/Layer 4 packet metadata, classify them using a lightweight machine-learning model, and prioritize them through Linux QoS mechanisms.

The design must support IPv4 and IPv6, TCP and UDP, encrypted application traffic, and bidirectional flow tracking.

Do not perform DPI, inspect application payloads, or depend on DNS/SNI signatures for classification.

